                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0143c4cf-a0d9-3df6-af6f-eacf1d811c23",
                        "entry_id": "4fe01742-2ba4-368b-b092-21e7b01da459",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sprachform/Mischsprache mit stark vereinfachter Grammatik und eingeschränktem Wortschatz, die bei Sprechern mit verschiedenen Muttersprachen ein notwendiges Minimum an Verständigung ermöglicht"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "48282336-6a82-4fde-b22c-65b0747dd127",
                                "sense_id": "0143c4cf-a0d9-3df6-af6f-eacf1d811c23",
                                "text": "Pidgins sind in Kolonialzeiten entstanden, um eine gewisse Verständigung zwischen Einheimischen und Händlern/Kolonisten zu ermöglichen. Pidgins sind Mischsprachen mit Bestandteilen aus den Sprachen der Kommunikationspartner."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fffd42fb-360f-4f96-b5fa-df139d09f77f",
                                "sense_id": "0143c4cf-a0d9-3df6-af6f-eacf1d811c23",
                                "text": "„Ihr Autor hatte sie mit krakeliger Schrift in einem abenteuerlichen Pidgin verfasst.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "671e82ff-07bc-4b5d-a7d1-533c3fa529d0",
                        "source_entry_id": "4fe01742-2ba4-368b-b092-21e7b01da459",
                        "source_sense_id": "0143c4cf-a0d9-3df6-af6f-eacf1d811c23",
                        "target_lang_word": "pidgin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pidgin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3843f70a-e80d-3dea-8eb8-b3d6ac5ece5c",
                                        "entry_id": "9fb6f373-971f-324f-aefd-edf0390cf5dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An amalgamation of two disparate languages, used by two populations having no common language as a lingua franca to communicate with each other, lacking formalized grammar and having a small, utilitarian vocabulary and no native speakers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "700e0fc2-97bb-40b6-b9b9-582413af6e75",
                                                "sense_id": "3843f70a-e80d-3dea-8eb8-b3d6ac5ece5c",
                                                "text": "‘I didnʼt know you can speak pidgin,’ he said and laughed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27f3df07-8970-3382-ad41-b4f2fac975f6",
                                        "entry_id": "9fb6f373-971f-324f-aefd-edf0390cf5dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person's business, occupation, work, or trade (also spelt as pigeon)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6795f76-1873-49e4-9eed-37e91f21cf1d",
                                                "sense_id": "27f3df07-8970-3382-ad41-b4f2fac975f6",
                                                "text": "Forget money. That's my pidgin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f51b5046-c84c-4597-bf21-23f3f56bde2d",
                                                "sense_id": "27f3df07-8970-3382-ad41-b4f2fac975f6",
                                                "text": "It's up to the detective sergeant to ask his own questions, that's not my pidgin. But I did wonder if either of you gentlemen had an idea of the exact time of the shot."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "67f0abb3-38ed-4f38-ab04-301ce4a6fe4e",
                        "source_entry_id": "4fe01742-2ba4-368b-b092-21e7b01da459",
                        "source_sense_id": "0143c4cf-a0d9-3df6-af6f-eacf1d811c23",
                        "target_lang_word": "pidgin",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pidgin",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04377c94-137d-3ce9-afd8-d49ba7c09f54",
                                        "entry_id": "ca61fdea-fd2d-3f58-b500-71e364d83c01",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Langage d’origine mixte, rudimentaire et utilisé par des personnes de langues maternelles différentes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f736c11-1fea-4ce5-bf00-130eea3516e4",
                                                "sense_id": "04377c94-137d-3ce9-afd8-d49ba7c09f54",
                                                "text": "On appelle généralement pidgin une langue simplifiée, créée à partir d’autres langues, et qui sert de langue véhiculaire pour des fins de commerce, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5a02c2d-49d3-3529-9226-5c86c2699a3f",
                                        "entry_id": "ca61fdea-fd2d-3f58-b500-71e364d83c01",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Langage d’origine mixte, sans égards à son niveau de complexité ou l’existence de locuteurs natifs. Sens employé dans les noms de langages."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "generally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d93806e4-e668-4aa2-bdee-ef5db96ce3f3",
                                                "sense_id": "f5a02c2d-49d3-3529-9226-5c86c2699a3f",
                                                "text": "Aujourd’hui, le pidgin du Nigeria, le nigerian pidgin english, est parlé par des dizaines de millions de gens, et il continue de progresser, mais il est toujours considéré, par les autorités, les universités, etc., comme quelque chose de condamnable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d6c8561-9479-325c-8962-6beda192147f",
                                        "entry_id": "ca61fdea-fd2d-3f58-b500-71e364d83c01",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Un pidgin précis, indiqué par le contexte."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "711f7b68-be88-429b-8dbe-02affaba0d08",
                                                "sense_id": "9d6c8561-9479-325c-8962-6beda192147f",
                                                "text": "Pas surprenant donc qu’un idiome commun ait émergé au fil du temps : le pidgin, un mélange d’anglais et de créole venus des Caraïbes et de portugais transmis par les navigateurs. — Il est juste question du pidgin du Nigéria. (AFP, Le pidgin, langue officieuse du Nigeria, 21 janvier 2014.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
